From 4167f972eb604d117a706859fe149c32677cfaa2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: w8 <w8@local>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 08:59:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] match.MANA_REGEN_STEP = client16402_floor_10000: the
 elixir unit is the game's 1/10000 and every regen step is floored

Mechanic: BattleState::new made one elixir lcm(MANA_REGEN_MS_1X, MANA_REGEN_MS_2X) = 28000 units and added 500 a tick at
1x (178.571 of the game's 1/10000) and 1000 at 2x (357.143), so the engine ran 0.32 % fast at 1x (one extra tick of regen
every ~312 ticks below the cap). New arm client16402_floor_10000 (shipped): one elixir = 10000 units and each step is
floor(TICK_MS x MAX_MANA x 10000 / regen_ms) = 178 / 357 / 537. Old arm exact_lcm; format-3 snapshots keep it, and every
snapshot carries its own unit and steps. The third rate already floored in the chosen unit.

Minimal reproduction: tests/mana_regen_step.rs: a battle with no play; every 1x step is 178 and every 2x step 357 of the
game's unit, and 6 -> 10 elixir fills on tick 225 (the exact rate's 224). Plant mana_regen_exact turns it red.

Parity-Evidence: ClashBot scratchpad/gauntlet/L74/parity/metrics (replay_metrics.py elixir, METRICS_J on rsfork_fin14c,
634 captured client 16.402 frame logs): open-loop own elixir within 0.1 on 0.840 of the frames (1x 0.911, 2x 0.751,
overtime 2x 0.730, 3x 0.683); the reader's own elixir rises 0.0178 / 0.0357 / 0.0537 a tick. The ledger's own
MANA_REGEN_MS_1X / _2X / _OVERTIME readings (truth.elixir_raw) give 178 / 357 / 537.

Hash continuity re-recorded at this change (ROYALESIM_RECORD_HASH_CONTINUITY=1, both tables): every battle's hash moves
from tick 0 because the elixir unit (part of the hashed state) is now 10000 a bar, and the regen steps are floored; no card
plays differently. state.rs mana_is_exact_over_a_full_bar now pins both arms (exact_lcm fills in 224 ticks, the shipped
arm in 225).
